# Last amended: 6th Sep, 2026

To work on crewai proceed as follows:
Open Ubuntu OR WSL-Ubuntu. Take following broad steps:

--- Broad Steps:
              --> In Console
                i)   Create Agents/Tasks and complete these
              --> In code .
               ii)   Set any creai-tools in respective Agent's jsonc file
              iii)   Set any custom-tools in respective Agent's jsonc file
               iv)   Write python file for the custom-tool under 'tools' folder
                v)   In 'crew.jsonc' file also add an embedder, as:
                      "embedder": {"provider": "ollama", "config": { "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest"}},
              --> In Console
               vi)   cd langchain_tools
                     crewai run
                     
                     Memory Error:
                     You may still get following memory_recall error.
                     Error: model "ollama/mistral:latest" not found, try pulling it first
                     (even though mistral:latest exists). Solution is not clear. Ignore
                     the error.
              
--- python files
       # 1.
       If working on python files:
              source /home/$USER/crewai_pjt/.venv/bin/activate 
              cd /home/$USER/crewai_pjt
              code . 
       
              # OR
                     . activate_crewai_pjt.sh
                     code .  
       
               When VScode is open: 
                     i)   click ctrl+shift+p to select Python interpreter
                     ii)  Python: Select Interpreter
                     iii) Look for crewai-pjt python environment.
       
       # 2.0
              After VSStudio is opened and python env for a file is selected
              keep cursor at the beginning of a function def and press
              'shift+ENTER' to execute the whole function-definition code.
              In the terminal below, start python, if not started.
       
       # 3.0 Execute python files from console in ubuntu shell, as:
       
              source /home/ashok/crewai_pjt/.venv/bin/activate 
              python  1.crewai_starter.py

-- Directly from Console

       # 4.0 Crew Creation (Console): 
              To create crew from Command line, there are two approaches:
       
              # Approach:1
              crewai create crew research_crew --classic
       
              This creates agents.yaml and tasks,yam files. Also creates 
              crew.py and main.py files. And also a sample file for custom-tools
              under 'tools' folder.
              Modify these files and run, as:
       
              cd research_crew
              crewai run
       
              # Approach:2
              crewai create crew research_crew
       
              This approach guides you to crew creation 
              step-by-step. Only, .jsonc files are created.
       
              No .py file (such as crew.py or main.py)
              is created. One .jsonc file is created for
              each Agent and for each Task. Agent .jsonc
              file, for example contains the ollama model
              specified and any crewai tool selected.
       
              And one file, crew.jsonc, is created that 
              describes our crew.
       
              We have now to read these files and amend as
              needed. For example, we may add custom-tools
              etc. No sample custom-tool.py is created. After
              everything is done, execute:
       
              cd research_crew
              crewai run

-- Missing packages

              If there are missing packages, install them
              WITHIN 'crewai_pjt/research_crew' folder 
              using 'uv add', as:

                     uv add <package1>  <package2>

